<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Omitted Details in <a href="#S1" title="1 Introduction ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Related Works</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Multi-agent LLM reasoning.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike LLM mixture-of-experts (MoE) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jacobs et al., 1991</a>, <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al., 2024</a>, <a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team, 2024</a>, <a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024</a>, <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dai et al., 2024</a>]</cite>, which is primarily motivated by engineering considerations, LLM aggregation focuses on ensembling the answers of different LLM agents in order to improve accuracy. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li [2024]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Elumar et al. [2025]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Subramaniam et al. [2025]</a></cite> simply use majority voting to aggregate.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Du et al. [2023]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lu et al. [2024]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. [2024]</a></cite> assign distinct roles to different LLMs, and then improve performance by exchanging response information among them.
Other lines of work instead focus on how to select among candidate outputs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al. [2023]</a></cite>.
Moreover, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. [2023a]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fu et al. [2025]</a></cite> demonstrate that aggregation of model outputs using confidence scores leads to significant improvements in accuracy, while <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tekin et al. [2024]</a></cite> tries to maximize model diversity. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fang et al. [2024]</a></cite> applies LLM aggregation to the e-commerce setting and learns optimal LLM weights based on product attributes. For a comprehensive overview, interested readers can refer to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. [2025]</a></cite>, which surveys reasoning approaches with multiple LLMs.
However, our work considers a different unsupervised learning setting, where no true labels are available, e.g., using different LLM agents to automatically annotate datasets. We propose a multi-agent LLM reasoning framework that leverages higher-order information structures, and we theoretically show that both first- and second-order information can effectively improve over zero-order majority voting, yielding optimal aggregation for one-round reasoning.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Information aggregation.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Information aggregation concerns how to combine noisy judgments in order to recover the truth. This line of work ranges from simple mechanisms like averaging and majority voting <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Penrose, 1946</a>, <a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tullock, 1959</a>]</cite>, to more recent algorithmic perspectives <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin and Chen, 2023</a>, <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2025</a>]</cite>. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Arieli et al. [2018]</a></cite> further develops a framework for identifying robust aggregators that perform well in the worst case without knowledge of the underlying information structure. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Neyman and Roughgarden [2022]</a></cite> extends this setting to continuous domains and shows that, under certain families, simple averaging is sufficiently good. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">De Oliveira et al. [2021]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Levy and Razin [2022]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Arieli et al. [2025]</a></cite> focus on environments with unknown correlations but known marginal distributions.
A complementary line of research leverages <em id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">second-order</em> information—agents’ beliefs about others’ answers—to improve aggregation. This thread originates with Bayesian Truth Serum <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Prelec, 2004</a>]</cite> and the “surprisingly popular” rule <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Prelec et al., 2017</a>]</cite>, and has since expanded to incorporate second- (and higher-) order signals in finite and potentially heterogeneous groups, both through theoretical analyses <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Palley and Soll, 2019</a>, <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2021</a>, <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Palley and Satopää, 2023</a>, <a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kong, 2024</a>, <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pan et al., 2024</a>]</cite> and empirical studies <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2021</a>, <a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Martinie et al., 2020</a>, <a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wilkening et al., 2022</a>]</cite>. Our work extends this literature to the setting of heterogeneous LLM experts by designing aggregation rules that exploit both first- and second-order information, thereby broadening the scope of information aggregation research beyond human judgments.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Omitted Details in <a href="#S2" title="2 Model ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Justification of Random Shuffling</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the simplicity of presentation, we use <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=2</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=(s_{1},s_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=(s_{1},s_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> to show the result, and then discuss how to extend it easily to a general <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Define two function families: <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{large}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{large}</annotation></semantics></math> is the original function family of all possible aggregation rules <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:S^{N}\rightarrow\Delta(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:S^{N}\rightarrow\Delta(S)</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{small}\subseteq F_{large}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{small}\subseteq F_{large}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes all functions <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</p>
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(a_{1},\cdots,a_{N})+f(1-a_{1},\cdots,1-a_{N})=1,\quad\text{for all }a_{1},\cdots,a_{N}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(a_{1},\cdots,a_{N})+f(1-a_{1},\cdots,1-a_{N})=1,\quad\text{for all }a_{1},\cdots,a_{N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> can be randomized, so we slightly abuse notation and use <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(a_{1},\cdots,a_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(a_{1},\cdots,a_{N})</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the probability that <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> outputs <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We use <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{large}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{large}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote a large joint distribution family that satisfies:</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Symmetry: For all <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{1}\mid S^{*}=s_{1})=\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{2}\mid S^{*}=s_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{1}\mid S^{*}=s_{1})=\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{2}\mid S^{*}=s_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Conditional Independence: <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{1},\cdots,A_{N}\mid S^{*})=\prod_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{P}(A_{i}\mid S^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{1},\cdots,A_{N}\mid S^{*})=\prod_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{P}(A_{i}\mid S^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We use <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{small}\subseteq P_{large}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{small}\subseteq P_{large}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote those <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math> that also satisfy the balance condition <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s_{1})=\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s_{2})=1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s_{1})=\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s_{2})=1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Assume we only know that the information structure <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\in P_{large}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\in P_{large}</annotation></semantics></math> and we hope to find a good aggregator. We hope to consider the worst-case scenario since we have no extra knowledge. The performance is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{f\in F_{large}}\max_{\mathbb{P}\in P_{large}}L(f,\mathbb{P})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{f\in F_{large}}\max_{\mathbb{P}\in P_{large}}L(f,\mathbb{P}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(f,\mathbb{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(f,\mathbb{P})</annotation></semantics></math> is the error probability of <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="L(f,\mathbb{P})\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{(S^{*},A_{1},\cdots,A_{N})\sim\mathbb{P}}\ind\{f(A_{1},\cdots,A_{N})\neq S^{*}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝟙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(f,\mathbb{P})\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{(S^{*},A_{1},\cdots,A_{N})\sim\mathbb{P}}\ind\{f(A_{1},\cdots,A_{N})\neq S^{*}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">If we perform random shuffle, the performance is analyzed as</p>
<table id="A2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{f\in F_{large}}\max_{\mathbb{P}\in P_{small}}L(f,\mathbb{P})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{f\in F_{large}}\max_{\mathbb{P}\in P_{small}}L(f,\mathbb{P}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For any aggregation function <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(a_{1},\cdots,a_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(a_{1},\cdots,a_{N})</annotation></semantics></math>, define the symmetric function</p>
<table id="A2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}(a_{1},\cdots,a_{N})\;=\;1-f(1-a_{1},\cdots,1-a_{N})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}(a_{1},\cdots,a_{N})\;=\;1-f(1-a_{1},\cdots,1-a_{N}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Equivalently, random shuffling can be seen as using <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. The resulting symmetrized rule lies in <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{small}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{small}</annotation></semantics></math>, so we can also write</p>
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{f\in F_{small}}\max_{\mathbb{P}\in P_{large}}L(f,\mathbb{P})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{f\in F_{small}}\max_{\mathbb{P}\in P_{large}}L(f,\mathbb{P}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{small}\subseteq F_{large}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{small}\subseteq F_{large}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{small}\subseteq P_{large}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{small}\subseteq P_{large}</annotation></semantics></math>, we always have</p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{f\in F_{small}}\max_{\mathbb{P}\in P_{large}}L(f,\mathbb{P})\;\geq\;\min_{f\in F_{large}}\max_{\mathbb{P}\in P_{large}}L(f,\mathbb{P})\;\geq\;\min_{f\in F_{large}}\max_{\mathbb{P}\in P_{small}}L(f,\mathbb{P})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{f\in F_{small}}\max_{\mathbb{P}\in P_{large}}L(f,\mathbb{P})\;\geq\;\min_{f\in F_{large}}\max_{\mathbb{P}\in P_{large}}L(f,\mathbb{P})\;\geq\;\min_{f\in F_{large}}\max_{\mathbb{P}\in P_{small}}L(f,\mathbb{P}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, viewing random shuffling as mixing <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}</annotation></semantics></math> shows that optimizing over <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{small}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{small}</annotation></semantics></math> against <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{large}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{large}</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent with <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{large}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{large}</annotation></semantics></math> against <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{small}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{small}</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining these observations yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{f\in F_{small}}\max_{\mathbb{P}\in P_{large}}L(f,\mathbb{P})\;=\;\min_{f\in F_{large}}\max_{\mathbb{P}\in P_{large}}L(f,\mathbb{P})\;=\;\min_{f\in F_{large}}\max_{\mathbb{P}\in P_{small}}L(f,\mathbb{P})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{f\in F_{small}}\max_{\mathbb{P}\in P_{large}}L(f,\mathbb{P})\;=\;\min_{f\in F_{large}}\max_{\mathbb{P}\in P_{large}}L(f,\mathbb{P})\;=\;\min_{f\in F_{large}}\max_{\mathbb{P}\in P_{small}}L(f,\mathbb{P}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore, in the worst case, there is no loss from considering random shuffling.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">For general <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, perform a random shuffle over all permutations <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> of the labels <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{1},\cdots,s_{K}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{1},\cdots,s_{K}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any permutation <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A2.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{m}(a_{1},\cdots,a_{N})\;=\;m^{-1}\!\left(f\bigl(m(a_{1}),\cdots,m(a_{N})\bigr)\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{m}(a_{1},\cdots,a_{N})\;=\;m^{-1}\!\left(f\bigl(m(a_{1}),\cdots,m(a_{N})\bigr)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">and draw <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly at random; the aggregator then uses <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> for aggregation. The same symmetrization argument applies as in the <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=2</annotation></semantics></math> case.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">For general <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, a symmetric condition is: for all <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq k</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{j}\mid S^{*}=s_{j})=x_{i},\qquad\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}\mid S^{*}=s_{j})=\frac{1-x_{i}}{K-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{j}\mid S^{*}=s_{j})=x_{i},\qquad\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}\mid S^{*}=s_{j})=\frac{1-x_{i}}{K-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">We need to assume the original distribution has the symmetry property. This roughly says that each agent has the same accuracy for all questions, which might not hold in the real world, but is a reasonable approximation when we cannot estimate per-question accuracies and instead only have overall accuracies <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for each agent <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Importantly, this symmetry is only needed for the justification here. After random shuffling, it holds by construction.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Omitted Details in <a href="#S3" title="3 Leveraging First-order Information ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3 Leveraging First-order Information ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first design a bijection between accuracies and a new vector <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> which represents agents’ ability. We assume <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}=\sigma_{K}(\beta_{i})=\frac{e^{\beta_{i}}}{K-1+e^{\beta_{i}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}=\sigma_{K}(\beta_{i})=\frac{e^{\beta_{i}}}{K-1+e^{\beta_{i}}}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. When the accuracy <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> increases, the agent’s corresponding ability <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> will be up as well. Then, due to the random shuffle, it’s equivalent to assume that <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=S^{*})=\frac{e^{\beta_{i}}}{K-1+e^{\beta_{i}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=S^{*})=\frac{e^{\beta_{i}}}{K-1+e^{\beta_{i}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{i}\neq S^{*})=\frac{K-1}{K-1+e^{\beta_{i}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{i}\neq S^{*})=\frac{K-1}{K-1+e^{\beta_{i}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">It then holds that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s_{i}|A_{1}=a_{1},...,A_{N}=a_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s_{i}|A_{1}=a_{1},...,A_{N}=a_{N})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=a_{1},...,A_{N}=a_{N}|S^{*}=s_{i})\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s_{i})}{\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=a_{1},...,A_{N}=a_{N})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=a_{1},...,A_{N}=a_{N}|S^{*}=s_{i})\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s_{i})}{\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=a_{1},...,A_{N}=a_{N})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\propto\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=a_{1},...,A_{N}=a_{N}|S^{*}=s_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=a_{1},...,A_{N}=a_{N}|S^{*}=s_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\prod_{j=1}^{N}\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=a_{j}|S^{*}=s_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\prod_{j=1}^{N}\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=a_{j}|S^{*}=s_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\prod_{j=1}^{N}[\frac{e^{\beta_{j}}}{K-1+e^{\beta_{j}}}\ind\{a_{j}=s_{i}\}+\frac{1}{K-1+e^{\beta_{j}}}\ind\{a_{j}\neq s_{i}\}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝟙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝟙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\prod_{j=1}^{N}[\frac{e^{\beta_{j}}}{K-1+e^{\beta_{j}}}\ind\{a_{j}=s_{i}\}+\frac{1}{K-1+e^{\beta_{j}}}\ind\{a_{j}\neq s_{i}\}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\prod_{j=1}^{N}\frac{e^{\beta_{j}\cdot\ind\{a_{j}=s_{i}\}+0\cdot\ind\{a_{j}\neq s_{i}\}}}{K-1+e^{\beta_{j}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝟙</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝟙</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\prod_{j=1}^{N}\frac{e^{\beta_{j}\cdot\ind\{a_{j}=s_{i}\}+0\cdot\ind\{a_{j}\neq s_{i}\}}}{K-1+e^{\beta_{j}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{e^{\sum_{\{j:a_{j}=s_{i}\}}\beta_{j}}}{\prod_{j=1}^{N}(K-1+e^{\beta_{j}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{e^{\sum_{\{j:a_{j}=s_{i}\}}\beta_{j}}}{\prod_{j=1}^{N}(K-1+e^{\beta_{j}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\propto e^{\sum_{\{j:a_{j}=s_{i}\}}\beta_{j}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∝</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto e^{\sum_{\{j:a_{j}=s_{i}\}}\beta_{j}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The second formula holds as <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s_{i})=\frac{1}{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s_{i})=\frac{1}{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{1},...,A_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{1},...,A_{N})</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. The second equation holds due to <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2 Model ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, and we have the third equation as agents are homogeneous with respect to incorrect options, say <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{i})=\frac{1}{K-1+e^{\beta_{i}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{i})=\frac{1}{K-1+e^{\beta_{i}}}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\neq s^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\neq s^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Since the Bayesian optimal aggregator chooses <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{s}=\argmax_{s}\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s|A_{1}=a_{1},...,A_{N}=a_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{s}=\argmax_{s}\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s|A_{1}=a_{1},...,A_{N}=a_{N})</annotation></semantics></math>, we only need to compare among <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{\{i:a_{i}=s\}}\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\{i:a_{i}=s\}}\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all labels. It’s equivalent to aggregate as</p>
<table id="A3.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{s}=\argmax_{s}\sum_{\{i:a_{i}=s\}}\beta_{i}=\argmax_{x}\sum_{\{i:a_{i}=s\}}\sigma_{K}^{-1}(x_{i})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></munder><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{s}=\argmax_{s}\sum_{\{i:a_{i}=s\}}\beta_{i}=\argmax_{x}\sum_{\{i:a_{i}=s\}}\sigma_{K}^{-1}(x_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">which finishes our proof.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary 1. ‣ 3 Leveraging First-order Information ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=2</annotation></semantics></math>, from the proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3 Leveraging First-order Information ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we immediately know that the optimal weight is <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{i}=\sigma_{2}^{-1}(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{i}=\sigma_{2}^{-1}(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{2}(x)=\frac{e^{x}}{1+e^{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{2}(x)=\frac{e^{x}}{1+e^{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> which is exactly the logistic function <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. It yields that the optimal weights are proportional to the logits of the accuracies, and closes off the proof.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmcorollary2" title="Corollary 2. ‣ 3 Leveraging First-order Information ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3 Leveraging First-order Information ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> proves that the optimal weights are proportional to the logits of the accuracies. When all agents are homogeneous, say <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}=x_{2}=\cdots=x_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}=x_{2}=\cdots=x_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, every weight becomes the same. Since the result of <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\argmax" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\argmax</annotation></semantics></math> is invariant to scaling, it’s equivalent to set all weights to 1, aligned with majority voting. Therefore, we prove that majority voting is the optimal strategy for homogeneous agents, justifying the use of majority voting for reasoning with a single model.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ 3 Leveraging First-order Information ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3 Leveraging First-order Information ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we already show that <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{OW}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{OW}</annotation></semantics></math> is Bayesian optimal. Therefore, when comparing <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{OW}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{OW}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}(a_{1},\cdots,a_{N})=a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}(a_{1},\cdots,a_{N})=a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we only need to figure out whether <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is Bayesian optimal.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">From <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Omitted Details in ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\addcontentsline{lla}{section}{\numberline q:posterior}\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s\mid A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N})=\frac{\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s)}{\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N})}\times\frac{e^{\sum_{\{j:a_{j}=s\}}\beta_{j}}}{\prod_{j=1}^{N}(K-1+e^{\beta_{j}})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\addcontentsline{lla}{section}{\numberline q:posterior}\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s\mid A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N})=\frac{\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s)}{\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N})}\times\frac{e^{\sum_{\{j:a_{j}=s\}}\beta_{j}}}{\prod_{j=1}^{N}(K-1+e^{\beta_{j}})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}=\sigma_{K}^{-1}(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}=\sigma_{K}^{-1}(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is Bayesian optimal, for any <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1},\cdots,a_{N},s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1},\cdots,a_{N},s</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(S^{*}=a_{i}\mid A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N})\geq P(S^{*}=s\mid A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(S^{*}=a_{i}\mid A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N})\geq P(S^{*}=s\mid A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Taking back to <a href="#A3.E8" title="In C.4 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Omitted Details in ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A3.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=a_{i})}{\prod_{j=1}^{N}(K-1+e^{\beta_{j}})}e^{\sum_{\{j:a_{j}=a_{i}\}}\beta_{j}}\geq\frac{\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s)}{\prod_{j=1}^{N}(K-1+e^{\beta_{j}})}e^{\sum_{\{j:a_{j}=s\}}\beta_{j}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=a_{i})}{\prod_{j=1}^{N}(K-1+e^{\beta_{j}})}e^{\sum_{\{j:a_{j}=a_{i}\}}\beta_{j}}\geq\frac{\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s)}{\prod_{j=1}^{N}(K-1+e^{\beta_{j}})}e^{\sum_{\{j:a_{j}=s\}}\beta_{j}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s)=\frac{1}{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s)=\frac{1}{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is then equivalent to</p>
<table id="A3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{\{j:a_{j}=a_{i}\}}\beta_{j}\geq\sum_{\{j:a_{j}=s\}}\beta_{j}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\{j:a_{j}=a_{i}\}}\beta_{j}\geq\sum_{\{j:a_{j}=s\}}\beta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.4" class="ltx_p">for any <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1},\cdots,a_{N},s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1},\cdots,a_{N},s</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> be any label except <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}=s\neq a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}=s\neq a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq i</annotation></semantics></math>.
It holds that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}\geq\sum_{j\neq i}\beta_{i}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}\geq\sum_{j\neq i}\beta_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">which concludes the proof.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Omitted Details in <a href="#S4" title="4 Leveraging Second-order Information ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Basic Properties of Second-order Information</h3>

<div id="Thmproposition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3</span></span><span id="Thmproposition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">After random shuffling, the second-order information has the following propositions.</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Exchangability: </span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{i}|A_{j})=\mathbb{P}(A_{j}|A_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{i}|A_{j})=\mathbb{P}(A_{j}|A_{i})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for every </span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Symmetry: </span><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{k})=\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{l}|A_{j}=s_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{k})=\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{l}|A_{j}=s_{l})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for every </span><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j,k,l)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j,k,l)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Monotonicity: If </span><math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}_{i}\geq x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}_{i}\geq x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, it holds that </span><math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\widetilde{A}_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{k})\geq\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\widetilde{A}_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{k})\geq\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{k})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for every </span><math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j,k)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Null information: If </span><math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}=\frac{1}{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}=\frac{1}{K}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, it holds that </span><math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{l})=\frac{1}{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{l})=\frac{1}{K}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for every </span><math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j,k,l)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j,k,l)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ D.1 Basic Properties of Second-order Information ‣ Appendix D Omitted Details in ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">From <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 2 Model ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we have <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s_{i})=\frac{1}{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s_{i})=\frac{1}{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{j}|S^{*}=s_{j})=x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{j}|S^{*}=s_{j})=x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|S^{*}=s_{j})=\frac{1-x_{i}}{K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|S^{*}=s_{j})=\frac{1-x_{i}}{K-1}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k}\neq s_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k}\neq s_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">For exchangability, it holds that if <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}=a_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=a_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, we’d have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=a_{i}|A_{j}=a_{j})=\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=a_{j}|A_{i}=a_{i})=x_{i}x_{j}+\frac{(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{K-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=a_{i}|A_{j}=a_{j})=\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=a_{j}|A_{i}=a_{i})=x_{i}x_{j}+\frac{(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{K-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\neq a_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\neq a_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=a_{i}|A_{j}=a_{j})=\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=a_{j}|A_{i}=a_{i})=\frac{x_{i}(1-x_{j})+(1-x_{i})x_{j}}{K-1}+\frac{(K-2)(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{(K-1)^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=a_{i}|A_{j}=a_{j})=\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=a_{j}|A_{i}=a_{i})=\frac{x_{i}(1-x_{j})+(1-x_{i})x_{j}}{K-1}+\frac{(K-2)(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{(K-1)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, it holds that <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=a_{i}|A_{j}=a_{j})=\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=a_{j}|A_{i}=a_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=a_{i}|A_{j}=a_{j})=\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=a_{j}|A_{i}=a_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For symmetry, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{k})=x_{i}x_{j}+\frac{(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{K-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{k})=x_{i}x_{j}+\frac{(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{K-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Note that this probability is independent of label <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>; therefore, we prove the property of symmetry.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For monotonicity, we know that when agent <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> has accuracy <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the required probability is</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{k})=x_{i}x_{j}+\frac{(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{K-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{k})=x_{i}x_{j}+\frac{(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{K-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">It then holds that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{k})}{\partial x_{i}}=x_{j}-\frac{1-x_{j}}{K-1}\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{k})}{\partial x_{i}}=x_{j}-\frac{1-x_{j}}{K-1}\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">The inequality holds because <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}\geq\frac{1}{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}\geq\frac{1}{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the monotonicity holds automatically.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For null information, there are two different cases. When <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k}=s_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k}=s_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{l})=x_{i}x_{j}+\frac{(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{K-1}=\frac{x_{j}}{K}+\frac{1-x_{j}}{K}=\frac{1}{K}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{l})=x_{i}x_{j}+\frac{(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{K-1}=\frac{x_{j}}{K}+\frac{1-x_{j}}{K}=\frac{1}{K}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, when <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k}\neq s_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k}\neq s_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that due to exchangability,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{l})=\frac{x_{i}(1-x_{j})+(1-x_{i})x_{j}}{K-1}+\frac{(K-2)(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{(K-1)^{2}}=\frac{1}{K}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{l})=\frac{x_{i}(1-x_{j})+(1-x_{i})x_{j}}{K-1}+\frac{(K-2)(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{(K-1)^{2}}=\frac{1}{K}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">It then finishes our proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmexample1" title="Example 1. ‣ 4.2 From Surprisingly Popular to Inverse Surprisingly Popular ‣ 4 Leveraging Second-order Information ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Example</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With some calculations, we notice that in the first 3 cases, the advantage of label <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is larger compared to <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for both <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SP</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ISP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ISP</annotation></semantics></math>. However, for the last case that <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{1},A_{2},A_{3},A_{4})=(s_{1},s_{1},s_{2},s_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{1},A_{2},A_{3},A_{4})=(s_{1},s_{1},s_{2},s_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, SP’s advantage of <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\frac{1}{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{1}{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, so SP will output <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. On the other hand, ISP’s advantage of <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, ISP will output <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> correctly. As MV breaks the tie uniformly, with probability <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, it will output correctly in case 4, while with another probability of <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the prediction will be wrong. Therefore, we know that the accuracies are <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{7}{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{7}{8}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{3}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{3}{4}</annotation></semantics></math> and 1 for MV, SP and ISP, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now give another example with an odd number of agents.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmexample3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmexample3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 3</span></span><span id="Thmexample3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmexample3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmexample3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmexample3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We assume there are 9 agents with accuracies <math id="Thmexample3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}=x_{2}=x_{3}=x_{4}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}=x_{2}=x_{3}=x_{4}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmexample3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{5}=x_{6}=x_{7}=x_{8}=x_{9}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{5}=x_{6}=x_{7}=x_{8}=x_{9}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmexample3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=2</annotation></semantics></math> candidates. We assume the true label after shuffling is <math id="Thmexample3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> without loss of generality because of symmetry. Since there are odd agents, there is no tie. Only in the case when <math id="Thmexample3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{5}=A_{6}=A_{7}=A_{8}=A_{9}=s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{5}=A_{6}=A_{7}=A_{8}=A_{9}=s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, MV will get a wrong aggregation with probability <math id="Thmexample3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{32}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>32</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{32}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For SP, when there are either 4 or 5 <math id="Thmexample3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the total score is the same as <math id="Thmexample3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{9}S_{SP}(s_{1},i)=\frac{21}{4}&gt;5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>9</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{9}S_{SP}(s_{1},i)=\frac{21}{4}&gt;5</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the probability of giving a wrong prediction is <math id="Thmexample3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{3}{16}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{3}{16}</annotation></semantics></math>. For ISP, however, the total score is only <math id="Thmexample3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{15}{4}&lt;4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{15}{4}&lt;4</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, ISP will output the correct prediction with probability 1 as there are at least 4 <math id="Thmexample3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 4.2 From Surprisingly Popular to Inverse Surprisingly Popular ‣ 4 Leveraging Second-order Information ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After random shuffling, we know that the prior over labels is a uniform distribution. Notice that <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Adv_{MV}(s^{*})=\sum_{i}\ind\{a_{i}=s^{*}\}-\frac{N}{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝟙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Adv_{MV}(s^{*})=\sum_{i}\ind\{a_{i}=s^{*}\}-\frac{N}{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. It holds that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[Adv_{MV}(s^{*})]=\sum_{i}x_{i}-\frac{N}{K}=\sum_{i}(x_{i}-\frac{1}{K})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[Adv_{MV}(s^{*})]=\sum_{i}x_{i}-\frac{N}{K}=\sum_{i}(x_{i}-\frac{1}{K}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let’s consider the first agent with accuracy <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, its contribution to <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[Adv_{MV}(s^{*})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[Adv_{MV}(s^{*})]</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}-\frac{1}{K}:=q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}-\frac{1}{K}:=q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Similarly, we can rephrase <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Adv_{ISP}(s^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Adv_{ISP}(s^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>. We first assume there are only two agents. When there are more than two agents, we need to take the average over the agents’ predictions that we condition on.
It holds with some calculations that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=s^{*})=x_{1}x_{2}+\frac{(1-x_{1})(1-x_{2})}{K-1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=s^{*})=x_{1}x_{2}+\frac{(1-x_{1})(1-x_{2})}{K-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and for any <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\neq s^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\neq s^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=s)=\frac{1}{K-1}x_{1}(1-x_{2})+\frac{1}{K-1}(1-x_{1})x_{2}+\frac{K-2}{(K-1)^{2}}(1-x_{1})(1-x_{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=s)=\frac{1}{K-1}x_{1}(1-x_{2})+\frac{1}{K-1}(1-x_{1})x_{2}+\frac{K-2}{(K-1)^{2}}(1-x_{1})(1-x_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Since for all <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\neq s^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\neq s^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> we have the same conditional probability, we use <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{1}=\neg s^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{1}=\neg s^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> to represent this probability with a little abuse of notations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the first agent has a contribution <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> of</p>
<table id="A4.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}-x_{2}\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=\neg s^{*})-(1-x_{2})[\frac{1}{K-1}\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=s^{*})+\frac{K-2}{K-1}\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=\neg s^{*})]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}-x_{2}\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=\neg s^{*})-(1-x_{2})[\frac{1}{K-1}\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=s^{*})+\frac{K-2}{K-1}\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=\neg s^{*})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">With probability <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the second agent will predict as <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. So, the corresponding conditional probability is <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=\neg s^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=\neg s^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>. On the other hand, with probability <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> will output another wrong answer. Then, within the <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K-1</annotation></semantics></math> possible exploration events, one is <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=s^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=s^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> while the other <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K-2</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=\neg s^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=\neg s^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We then calculate the gap between <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. We notice that either <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}=\frac{1}{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}=\frac{1}{K}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}=\frac{1}{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}=\frac{1}{K}</annotation></semantics></math> will lead to zero gap due to <a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ D.1 Basic Properties of Second-order Information ‣ Appendix D Omitted Details in ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. It then holds that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{2}-q_{1}=\frac{1}{(K-1)^{3}}(x_{1}-\frac{1}{K})(Kx_{2}-1)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{2}-q_{1}=\frac{1}{(K-1)^{3}}(x_{1}-\frac{1}{K})(Kx_{2}-1)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, when there are more than two agents, the weight of each agent in the contribution <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which yields that the difference between agent 1’s contributions to ISP and MV is now</p>
<table id="A4.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=2}^{N}\frac{1}{N-1}\frac{1}{(K-1)^{3}}(x_{1}-\frac{1}{K})(Kx_{i}-1)^{2}=\sum_{i=2}^{N}\frac{1}{N-1}\frac{1}{K(K-1)^{3}}(Kx_{1}-1)(Kx_{i}-1)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=2}^{N}\frac{1}{N-1}\frac{1}{(K-1)^{3}}(x_{1}-\frac{1}{K})(Kx_{i}-1)^{2}=\sum_{i=2}^{N}\frac{1}{N-1}\frac{1}{K(K-1)^{3}}(Kx_{1}-1)(Kx_{i}-1)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Recall that the total advantage is the sum of every agent’s contribution. It then holds that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[Adv_{ISP}(s^{*})-Adv_{MV}(s^{*})]=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j\in[N]\setminus\{i\}}(Kx_{i}-1)(Kx_{j}-1)^{2}}{(N-1)K(K-1)^{3}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[Adv_{ISP}(s^{*})-Adv_{MV}(s^{*})]=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j\in[N]\setminus\{i\}}(Kx_{i}-1)(Kx_{j}-1)^{2}}{(N-1)K(K-1)^{3}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p">due to the linearity of the expectation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For any fixed accuracies <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},...,x_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},...,x_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, we notice that the numerator is proportional to <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(N^{2}K^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(N^{2}K^{3})</annotation></semantics></math> and the denominator is roughly <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(NK^{4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(NK^{4})</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we know that <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[Adv_{ISP}(s^{*})-Adv_{MV}(s^{*})]\eqsim\Theta(\frac{N}{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[Adv_{ISP}(s^{*})-Adv_{MV}(s^{*})]\eqsim\Theta(\frac{N}{K})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the advantage is the sum of every agent’s contribution, it’s reasonable to be proportional to <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>.
More notably, the advantage of ISP over MV is proportional to <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, as the number of options <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> increases, the performance gap between them diminishes. This is because ISP motivates agents to reflect on alternative options in order to explore the unknown environment. However, as <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> grows, since we only conduct a single round of uniform reflection, i.e., computing the conditional probability given <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\neg A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\neg A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the probability of reaching the correct answer is roughly <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{K}</annotation></semantics></math> if the original prediction is wrong. As a result, the benefit of ISP relative to MV is most significant in the region of a few options. For tasks with many possible options or open-ended problems, such as text generation, we may need to design additional reflection or exploration mechanisms, which we leave for future work.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For SP, we also presume there are <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=2</annotation></semantics></math> agents. So, the contribution of the first agent is now</p>
<table id="A4.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}-x_{2}\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=s^{*})-(1-x_{2})\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=\neg s^{*}):=q_{3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}-x_{2}\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=s^{*})-(1-x_{2})\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s^{*}|A_{2}=\neg s^{*}):=q_{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">This is because agent 2 will predict <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and answer mistakenly with another probability <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, we only need to compute the gap between <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}-q_{3}=\frac{(Kx_{1}-1)(Kx_{2}-1)^{2}}{K(K-1)^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}-q_{3}=\frac{(Kx_{1}-1)(Kx_{2}-1)^{2}}{K(K-1)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p">When there are more than two agents, the gap would become</p>
<table id="A4.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{K}-S_{SP}(s^{*},1)=\frac{\sum_{i=2}^{N}(Kx_{1}-1)(Kx_{i}-1)^{2}}{(N-1)K(K-1)^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{K}-S_{SP}(s^{*},1)=\frac{\sum_{i=2}^{N}(Kx_{1}-1)(Kx_{i}-1)^{2}}{(N-1)K(K-1)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.4" class="ltx_p">Therefore, adding the difference of all agents yields</p>
<table id="A4.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[Adv_{MV}(s^{*})-Adv_{SP}(s^{*})]=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j\in[N]\setminus\{i\}}(Kx_{i}-1)(Kx_{j}-1)^{2}}{(N-1)K(K-1)^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[Adv_{MV}(s^{*})-Adv_{SP}(s^{*})]=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j\in[N]\setminus\{i\}}(Kx_{i}-1)(Kx_{j}-1)^{2}}{(N-1)K(K-1)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike the gap between ISP and MV, this gap is <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(N)</annotation></semantics></math> with increasing option number <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> for any fixed <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},...,x_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},...,x_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. This shows that SP is consistently weaker than MV by a constant factor. The reason is that when each agent answers incorrectly with some fixed probability, it tends to get stuck on the wrong option, rather than reflecting on how other agents would behave under alternative predictions as ISP does. As a result, its performance can be even worse than simple majority voting. This demonstrates that the surprising popularity mechanism, originally designed for incentive settings, is not suitable for LLM aggregation scenarios, where agents have no incentive to deliberately provide incorrect answers.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">We further observe that as model accuracy <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> improves, both gaps increase accordingly. Nevertheless, because higher model accuracy inherently elevates the likelihood that all three methods converge to the correct prediction, the relative improvement of ISP over MV may exhibit a more nuanced and non-monotonic behavior. We leave a deeper characterization of this phenomenon to future work.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, since we know that every agent is better than a random predictor, say <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\geq\frac{1}{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\geq\frac{1}{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[Adv_{ISP}(s^{*})]\geq\mathbb{E}[Adv_{MV}(s^{*})]\geq\mathbb{E}[Adv_{SP}(s^{*})]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[Adv_{ISP}(s^{*})]\geq\mathbb{E}[Adv_{MV}(s^{*})]\geq\mathbb{E}[Adv_{SP}(s^{*})],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p">which ends the proof. Note that, due to symmetry, whenever <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>
has a larger advantage, other labels <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\neg s^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\neg s^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> must necessarily have smaller advantages. Therefore, compared to MV and SP, ISP is more likely to identify that label <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> possesses the greater advantage, and thus aggregate toward the correct prediction of the ground truth label.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 4.3 Practical Estimation of Second-order Information ‣ 4 Leveraging Second-order Information ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We notice that after a random shuffle, the expectation of the advantage of ISP equals</p>
<table id="A4.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[Adv_{ISP}(s^{*})]=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left[x_{i}-\frac{1}{(N-1)(K-1)}\sum_{j\in[N]\setminus\{i\}}\mathbb{E}[\sum_{s}\ind\{a_{j}=s\}\sum_{\widetilde{s}\in\neg s}\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})]\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>s</mi></munder><mi>𝟙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[Adv_{ISP}(s^{*})]=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left[x_{i}-\frac{1}{(N-1)(K-1)}\sum_{j\in[N]\setminus\{i\}}\mathbb{E}[\sum_{s}\ind\{a_{j}=s\}\sum_{\widetilde{s}\in\neg s}\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})]\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">due to the linearity of expectation. Therefore, we only need to bound the distance between <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\ind\{a_{j}=s\}\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝟙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\ind\{a_{j}=s\}\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=s|S^{*}=s^{*})\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=s|S^{*}=s^{*})\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})</annotation></semantics></math> for any pair <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,\widetilde{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,\widetilde{s})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We know that <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\ind\{a_{j}=s\}]=\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=s|S^{*}=s^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝟙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\ind\{a_{j}=s\}]=\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=s|S^{*}=s^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> when the true label is <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the only issue is that <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\ind\{a_{j}=s\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝟙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ind\{a_{j}=s\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})</annotation></semantics></math> are correlated. Assuming we have <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. questions, we now consider the aggregation for the <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-th question, and we use the subscript <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-m</annotation></semantics></math> to represent all questions except the <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-th one. <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}</annotation></semantics></math> means that we exclude the <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-th question when computing the empirical conditional probability. Therefore, it holds that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle|\mathbb{E}[\ind\{a_{j}=s\}\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})]-\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=s|S^{*}=s^{*})\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝟙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\mathbb{E}[\ind\{a_{j}=s\}\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})]-\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=s|S^{*}=s^{*})\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex64.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle|\mathbb{E}[\ind\{a_{j}=s\}\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})]-\mathbb{E}[\ind\{a_{j}=s\}\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})]|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝟙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝟙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\mathbb{E}[\ind\{a_{j}=s\}\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})]-\mathbb{E}[\ind\{a_{j}=s\}\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})]|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+|\mathbb{E}[\ind\{a_{j}=s\}\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})]-\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=s|S^{*}=s^{*})\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝟙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+|\mathbb{E}[\ind\{a_{j}=s\}\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})]-\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=s|S^{*}=s^{*})\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex66.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})-\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})-\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+|\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=s|S^{*}=s^{*})\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})-\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=s|s^{*})\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+|\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=s|S^{*}=s^{*})\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})-\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=s|s^{*})\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})-\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|+|\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})-\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})-\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|+|\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})-\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The first inequality holds due to the triangle inequality, while the second one holds as <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="0\leq\ind\{a_{j}=s\}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝟙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\ind\{a_{j}=s\}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}</annotation></semantics></math>. The third inequality holds due to <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=s|S^{*}=s^{*})\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=s|S^{*}=s^{*})\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For the term <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})-\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})-\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|</annotation></semantics></math>, recall that <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})=\frac{\#\{A_{i}=s^{*},A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}}{\#\{A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})=\frac{\#\{A_{i}=s^{*},A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}}{\#\{A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})=\frac{\#_{-m}\{A_{i}=s^{*},A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}}{\#_{-m}\{A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>#</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>#</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})=\frac{\#_{-m}\{A_{i}=s^{*},A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}}{\#_{-m}\{A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using Hoeffding’s inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wainwright, 2019</a>]</cite>, it holds that with probability at least <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\mathcal{O}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\mathcal{O}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\addcontentsline{lla}{section}{\numberline neq:first}|\#\{A_{i}=s^{*},A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}-M\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s^{*},A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|\lesssim\mathcal{O}(\sqrt{M\log(\frac{1}{\delta})})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\addcontentsline{lla}{section}{\numberline neq:first}|\#\{A_{i}=s^{*},A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}-M\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s^{*},A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|\lesssim\mathcal{O}(\sqrt{M\log(\frac{1}{\delta})}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\addcontentsline{lla}{section}{\numberline neq:second}|\#\{A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}-M\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|\lesssim\mathcal{O}(\sqrt{M\log(\frac{1}{\delta})})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>#</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≲</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\addcontentsline{lla}{section}{\numberline neq:second}|\#\{A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}-M\mathbb{P}(A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|\lesssim\mathcal{O}(\sqrt{M\log(\frac{1}{\delta})}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">In addition, we know that <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\#\{A_{i}=s^{*},A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}-\#_{-m}\{A_{i}=s^{*},A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>#</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\#\{A_{i}=s^{*},A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}-\#_{-m}\{A_{i}=s^{*},A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\#\{A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}-\#_{-m}\{A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>#</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>#</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\#\{A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}-\#_{-m}\{A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. It then holds that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})-\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|\lesssim\mathcal{O}(\frac{1}{M})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})-\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|\lesssim\mathcal{O}(\frac{1}{M}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.4" class="ltx_p">when <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\gtrsim\Omega(\log(\frac{1}{\delta}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≳</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\gtrsim\Omega(\log(\frac{1}{\delta}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For the second term <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})-\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})-\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|</annotation></semantics></math>, by replacing <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\#\{A_{i}=s^{*},A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\#\{A_{i}=s^{*},A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\#\{A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>#</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\#\{A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\#_{-m}\{A_{i}=s^{*},A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>#</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\#_{-m}\{A_{i}=s^{*},A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\#_{-m}\{A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>#</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\#_{-m}\{A_{j}=\widetilde{s}\}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively in Inequalities <a href="#A4.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ D.4 Proof of ‣ Appendix D Omitted Details in ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> and <a href="#A4.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ D.4 Proof of ‣ Appendix D Omitted Details in ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, it then holds that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})-\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|\lesssim\mathcal{O}(\sqrt{\frac{1}{M}\log(\frac{1}{\delta})})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{-m}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})-\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s^{*}|A_{j}=\widetilde{s})|\lesssim\mathcal{O}(\sqrt{\frac{1}{M}\log(\frac{1}{\delta})}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">when <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we know that with probability at least <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\Theta(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\Theta(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>, for every question, it holds that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathbb{E}[\widehat{Adv}_{ISP}(s^{*})]-\mathbb{E}[{Adv}_{ISP}(s^{*})]|\lesssim\widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(\sqrt{\frac{1}{M}\log(\frac{1}{\delta})})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathbb{E}[\widehat{Adv}_{ISP}(s^{*})]-\mathbb{E}[{Adv}_{ISP}(s^{*})]|\lesssim\widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(\sqrt{\frac{1}{M}\log(\frac{1}{\delta})}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Here, we have <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> questions in total, so the cumulative failure probability is polynomial in <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, we use <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> to hide some logarithmic terms of <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> in the concentration upper bound.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Together with <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 4.2 From Surprisingly Popular to Inverse Surprisingly Popular ‣ 4 Leveraging Second-order Information ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and choosing the constant before the failure probability <math id="A4.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> elaborately, it yields that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\widehat{Adv}_{ISP}(s^{*})-Adv_{MV}(s^{*})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\widehat{Adv}_{ISP}(s^{*})-Adv_{MV}(s^{*})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex72.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}[{Adv}_{ISP}(s^{*})-Adv_{MV}(s^{*})]-|\mathbb{E}[\widehat{Adv}_{ISP}(s^{*})-Adv_{ISP}(s^{*})]|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}[{Adv}_{ISP}(s^{*})-Adv_{MV}(s^{*})]-|\mathbb{E}[\widehat{Adv}_{ISP}(s^{*})-Adv_{ISP}(s^{*})]|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gtrsim\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j\in[N]\setminus\{i\}}(Kx_{i}-1)(Kx_{j}-1)^{2}}{(N-1)K(K-1)^{3}}-\widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(\sqrt{\frac{1}{{M}}\log(\frac{1}{\delta})})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≳</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gtrsim\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j\in[N]\setminus\{i\}}(Kx_{i}-1)(Kx_{j}-1)^{2}}{(N-1)K(K-1)^{3}}-\widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(\sqrt{\frac{1}{{M}}\log(\frac{1}{\delta})}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p6.2" class="ltx_p">which ends the proof.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Omitted Details in <a href="#S5" title="5 Experiments ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Omitted Details in <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1 Evaluation on Simulated Data ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the implementation of MV, we break ties randomly, and this procedure has little effect on the overall results.
In <a href="#A5.F1" title="In E.1 Omitted Details in ‣ Appendix E Omitted Details in ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we observe that as the number of choices <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> increases, the gap between ISP and MV gradually decreases, validating <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 4.2 From Surprisingly Popular to Inverse Surprisingly Popular ‣ 4 Leveraging Second-order Information ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. At the same time, the gap between MV and SP first decreases and then stabilizes. This initial reduction arises because, as <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> grows, the accuracies of all three algorithms improve, thereby reducing the potential for further gains. Decomposing the factors that contribute to the decrease is an interesting direction for future research.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.01499v1/iclr2026/figures/ISP.png" id="A5.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/158;" width="238" height="158" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>The performance gap between ISP and MV vanishes as <math id="A5.F1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> increases.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Omitted Details in <a href="#S5.SS2" title="5.2 Adapted Optimal Weight Algorithm Without Ground Truth ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With some calculations, it holds that</p>
<table id="A5.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{l})[x_{1},...,x_{N}]=\begin{cases}x_{i}x_{j}+\frac{(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{K-1},&amp;\text{if }s_{k}=s_{l},\\
\frac{x_{i}(1-x_{j})+(1-x_{i})x_{j}}{K-1}+\frac{(K-2)(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{(K-1)^{2}},&amp;\text{if }s_{k}\neq s_{l}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{l})[x_{1},...,x_{N}]=\begin{cases}x_{i}x_{j}+\frac{(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{K-1},&amp;\text{if }s_{k}=s_{l},\\
\frac{x_{i}(1-x_{j})+(1-x_{i})x_{j}}{K-1}+\frac{(K-2)(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{(K-1)^{2}},&amp;\text{if }s_{k}\neq s_{l}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Together with <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{l})=\frac{\#\{A_{i}=s_{k},A_{j}=s_{l}\}}{\#\{A_{j}=s_{l}\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbb{P}}(A_{i}=s_{k}|A_{j}=s_{l})=\frac{\#\{A_{i}=s_{k},A_{j}=s_{l}\}}{\#\{A_{j}=s_{l}\}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can use some gradient descent method to solve <a href="#S5.E7" title="In 5.2 Adapted Optimal Weight Algorithm Without Ground Truth ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, which yields</p>
<table id="A5.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{x}_{1},...,\widehat{x}_{N}=\argmin_{x_{1},...,x_{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{x}_{1},...,\widehat{x}_{N}=\argmin_{x_{1},...,x_{N}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex75.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Big[\sum_{i,j,k}(x_{i}x_{j}+\frac{(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{K-1}-\frac{\#\{A_{i}=s_{k},A_{j}=s_{k}\}}{\#\{A_{j}=s_{k}\}})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big[\sum_{i,j,k}(x_{i}x_{j}+\frac{(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{K-1}-\frac{\#\{A_{i}=s_{k},A_{j}=s_{k}\}}{\#\{A_{j}=s_{k}\}})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{i,j,k,l:k\neq l}(\frac{x_{i}(1-x_{j})+(1-x_{i})x_{j}}{K-1}+\frac{(K-2)(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{(K-1)^{2}}-\frac{\#\{A_{i}=s_{k},A_{j}=s_{l}\}}{\#\{A_{j}=s_{l}\}})^{2}\Big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{i,j,k,l:k\neq l}(\frac{x_{i}(1-x_{j})+(1-x_{i})x_{j}}{K-1}+\frac{(K-2)(1-x_{i})(1-x_{j})}{(K-1)^{2}}-\frac{\#\{A_{i}=s_{k},A_{j}=s_{l}\}}{\#\{A_{j}=s_{l}\}})^{2}\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We can also explore alternative loss functions rather than squared loss here, which we leave as a direction for future research.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Omitted Details in <a href="#S5.SS3" title="5.3 Real-world Datasets ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the GPT family, we access the models exclusively through the Microsoft Azure API, using the default template with
temperature=1.0 and
top_p=1.0. For the other open-source models, we generate responses on a single A100 GPU using vLLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwon et al., 2023</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The UltraFeedback dataset contains 63,135 questions. We retain only those that comply with OpenAI’s content management policy, with 56,380 left. For each retained question, we randomly shuffle the two candidate responses and query different LLM agents using the following prompt template. We instruct the LLMs to provide only the final answer without any explanation, which facilitates cleaner data processing. While prompt engineering may further improve the accuracy of individual model responses, we leave this as an interesting direction for future research.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para"><pre id="A5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
**UltraFeedback prompt**: You are a helpful assistant.
Original question, e.g., "Prompt: how can i develop a habit of drawing daily".
There are two answers:
A. One response, e.g., "Developing a daily habit of drawing can be challenging but with consistent practice and a few tips, it can become an enjoyable and rewarding part of your daily routine. Here are some strategies to help you develop the habit of drawing daily..."
B. The other response, e.g., "As an AI language model, I cannot personally develop habits for you. But, here are some tips for developing a habit of drawing daily..."
Which answer is better? Reply with only 'A' or 'B'. Do not explain or repeat the answers.
</pre>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The MMLU dataset contains 115,700 questions. Among them, 109,820 questions are successfully answered by all LLMs. For each question, we first randomly shuffle the four answer choices. We then query the models using the following prompt template.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para"><pre id="A5.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
**MMLU prompt**: You are a helpful assistant.
Original question, e.g., "A little stress is good, since it helps you keep motivated to meet your goals. However, too much stress is bad for your health...According to the passage, which of the following is NOT true?"
There are four options.
A. One option, e.g., "It's unnecessary for you to do all the tasks by yourself."
B. One option, e.g., "It helps you stay motivated to think about the undone tasks."
C. One option, e.g., "It helps if you put your attention to one task at a time."
D. One option, e.g., "It's better to plan a specific time to do the task."
Which option is correct? Reply with only 'A', 'B', 'C', or 'D'. Do not explain or repeat the answer."
</pre>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The ARMMAN dataset contains health information and call records for 12,000 women. 11,785 cases are successfully answered by all LLMs. We treat a call as valid if its duration exceeds ten seconds. We provide the LLMs with the call reception records from the past ten weeks, and then query the models using the following simple prompt template.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para"><pre id="A5.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
**ARMMAN prompt**: You are a helpful assistant.
Brief introduction, e.g., "You are a mother enrolled in the ARMMAN Maternal and Child Healthcare Mobile Health program. ARMMAN is a nongovernmental organization in India dedicated to reducing maternal and neonatal mortality among underprivileged communities..."
Your Background: e.g., "You enrolled in the program during the 9 week of your pregnancy. You are 35+ years old...You have had 0 stillbirth(s) and have 2 living child(ren)."
Past Behavior: e.g., "The following is a record of your previous listening behavior (each representing one week): - Week 1: Listened for 0 seconds, Receive an automated voice message...- Week 10: Listened for 0 seconds, Receive an automated voice message"
This Week's Call Type: e.g., "You will receive an automated voice message this week."
Task, e.g., "Based on this information, as well as the context of the program and on typical behavior of mothers in India, decide whether you will be engaged with the next health message..."
Question: e.g., "Will you be engaged with the next health message (listening for at least 10 seconds)?"
Instruction, e.g., "Please decide whether you will be engaged with the next health message: '##Yes##' for engagement (listening at least 10 seconds) or '##No##' for lack of engagement (listening less than 10 seconds) in this week."
There are two answers:
A. One option, e.g., "##Yes##"
B. The other option, e.g., "##No##"
Which answer is better? Reply with only 'A' or 'B'. Do not explain or repeat the answers."
</pre>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover, we find that the distribution of answers from the selected models is nearly uniform over the candidates, indicating minimal position effects. Therefore, we conclude that random shuffling does not affect the model responses significantly.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.4 </span>Omitted Details in <a href="#S5.SS4" title="5.4 Evaluation Results on Real-World Datasets ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Within each family, we use “S” to denote the strong model and “W” to denote the weak model. Accordingly, we abbreviate
GPT-4o-2024-11-20, GPT-35-turbo-0125, Qwen2.5-Instruct-14B, Qwen2.5-Instruct-3B, Llama3.1-8B-Instruct, Llama3.2-1B-Instruct, Phi-4 and Phi-4-mini-instruct as GS, GW, QS, QW, LS, LW, PS and PW, respectively. We begin by presenting in <a href="#A5.F2" title="In E.4 Omitted Details in ‣ Appendix E Omitted Details in ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> the overall performance of these eight models on UltraFeedback, MMLU, and ARMMAN.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.01499v1/iclr2026/figures/model.png" id="A5.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/188;" width="476" height="188" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Accuracy of different LLMs across the three datasets.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now present the results of the 16 ensembles on UltraFeedback in <a href="#A5.T4" title="In E.4 Omitted Details in ‣ Appendix E Omitted Details in ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. We observe that MV outperforms ISP only in the case of aggregating GPT-4o-2024-11-20, Qwen2.5-Instruct-3B, Llama3.2-1B-Instruct and Phi-4. In all other cases, our three algorithms achieve higher accuracy than MV.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T4" class="ltx_table">
