<div id="A5.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we present the experimental results on the ARMMAN dataset. From <a href="#A5.T6" title="In E.4 Omitted Details in ‣ Appendix E Omitted Details in ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we observe that when selecting GPT-35-turbo-0125, Qwen2.5-Instruct-14B, Llama3.2-1B-Instruct and Phi-4-mini-instruct, OW-L underperforms MV. Similarly, when selecting GPT-35-turbo-0125, Qwen2.5-Instruct-3B, Llama3.2-1B-Instruct and Phi-4, OW-I underperforms MV. Moreover, MV outperforms both OW-I and ISP when selecting GPT-35-turbo-0125, Qwen2.5-Instruct-3B, Llama3.1-8B-Instruct and Phi-4-mini-instruct. In all remaining cases, however, our three algorithms achieve higher accuracy than MV.</p>
</div>
