<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Omitted Details in <a href="#S6" title="6 Extension: Beyond Conditional Independence ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></h2>

<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 6 Extension: Beyond Conditional Independence ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1},\cdots,a_{N},s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1},\cdots,a_{N},s</annotation></semantics></math>, We now have</p>
<table id="A6.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s\mid A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s\mid A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex77.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N}\mid S^{*}=s)\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s)}{\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N}\mid S^{*}=s)\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s)}{\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\alpha\sim D(\alpha)}\frac{\prod_{i:a_{i}=s}e^{\alpha\beta_{i}}}{\prod_{i=1}^{N}(K-1+e^{\alpha\beta_{i}})}\times\frac{\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s)}{{\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∏</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\alpha\sim D(\alpha)}\frac{\prod_{i:a_{i}=s}e^{\alpha\beta_{i}}}{\prod_{i=1}^{N}(K-1+e^{\alpha\beta_{i}})}\times\frac{\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s)}{{\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\alpha\sim D(\alpha)}\frac{\prod_{i:a_{i}=s}e^{\alpha\beta_{i}}}{\prod_{i=1}^{N}(K-1+e^{\alpha\beta_{i}})}\times\frac{\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s)}{{\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∏</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\alpha\sim D(\alpha)}\frac{\prod_{i:a_{i}=s}e^{\alpha\beta_{i}}}{\prod_{i=1}^{N}(K-1+e^{\alpha\beta_{i}})}\times\frac{\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s)}{{\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\alpha\sim D(\alpha)}\frac{e^{\alpha\sum_{i:a_{i}=s}\beta_{i}}}{\prod_{i=1}^{N}(K-1+e^{\alpha\beta_{i}})}\times\frac{\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s)}{{\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N})}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\alpha\sim D(\alpha)}\frac{e^{\alpha\sum_{i:a_{i}=s}\beta_{i}}}{\prod_{i=1}^{N}(K-1+e^{\alpha\beta_{i}})}\times\frac{\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s)}{{\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=a_{1},\cdots,A_{N}=a_{N})}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since the Bayesian optimal aggregator chooses <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{s}=\argmax_{s}\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s|A_{1}=a_{1},...,A_{N}=a_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{s}=\argmax_{s}\mathbb{P}(S^{*}=s|A_{1}=a_{1},...,A_{N}=a_{N})</annotation></semantics></math>,
we then only need to compare among <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{i:a_{i}=s}\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i:a_{i}=s}\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>. It is equivalent to aggregate as</p>
<table id="A6.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{s}=\argmax_{s\in S}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta_{i}\ind\{a_{i}=s\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝟙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{s}=\argmax_{s\in S}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta_{i}\ind\{a_{i}=s\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which concludes the proof.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5. ‣ 6 Extension: Beyond Conditional Independence ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now show that, with the existence of <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, it still holds that ISP outperforms MV, which in turn outperforms SP.
Note that we assume we don’t know the difficulty level <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> for each question; otherwise, we can always group questions with the same <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. We study the case where there are only two labels. We use <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the accuracy under difficulty <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, we have the following equations,</p>
<table id="A6.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s_{i}|A_{2}=s_{j})=\mathbb{E}_{D(\alpha)}\frac{x_{1}(\alpha)(1-x_{2}(\alpha))+(1-x_{1}(\alpha))x_{2}(\alpha)}{K-1}+\frac{K-2}{(K-1)^{2}}(1-x_{1}(\alpha)(1-x_{2}(\alpha)))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s_{i}|A_{2}=s_{j})=\mathbb{E}_{D(\alpha)}\frac{x_{1}(\alpha)(1-x_{2}(\alpha))+(1-x_{1}(\alpha))x_{2}(\alpha)}{K-1}+\frac{K-2}{(K-1)^{2}}(1-x_{1}(\alpha)(1-x_{2}(\alpha))),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">for any <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\neq s_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\neq s_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A6.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s_{i}|A_{2}=s_{i})=\mathbb{E}_{D(\alpha)}x_{1}(\alpha)x_{2}(\alpha)+\frac{(1-x_{1}(\alpha))(1-x_{2}(\alpha))}{K-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(A_{1}=s_{i}|A_{2}=s_{i})=\mathbb{E}_{D(\alpha)}x_{1}(\alpha)x_{2}(\alpha)+\frac{(1-x_{1}(\alpha))(1-x_{2}(\alpha))}{K-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Recall that for any question, we use <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the true label. For this question, due to the linearity of the expectation, we only need to prove that for any <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A6.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex84.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{2}(\alpha)[\frac{x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime})(1-x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime}))+(1-x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime}))x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime})}{K-1}+\frac{K-2}{(K-1)^{2}}(1-x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime})(1-x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime})))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{2}(\alpha)[\frac{x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime})(1-x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime}))+(1-x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime}))x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime})}{K-1}+\frac{K-2}{(K-1)^{2}}(1-x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime})(1-x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime})))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1-x_{2}(\alpha)}{K-1}[x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime})x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime})+\frac{(1-x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime}))(1-x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime}))}{K-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1-x_{2}(\alpha)}{K-1}[x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime})x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime})+\frac{(1-x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime}))(1-x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime}))}{K-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+(1-x_{2}(\alpha))\frac{K-2}{K-1}[\frac{x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime})(1-x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime}))+(1-x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime}))x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime})}{K-1}+\frac{K-2}{(K-1)^{2}}(1-x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime})(1-x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime})))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(1-x_{2}(\alpha))\frac{K-2}{K-1}[\frac{x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime})(1-x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime}))+(1-x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime}))x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime})}{K-1}+\frac{K-2}{(K-1)^{2}}(1-x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime})(1-x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime})))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{1}{K}\leq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{1}{K}\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}=\frac{e^{\alpha\beta_{i}}}{e^{\alpha\beta_{i}}+K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}=\frac{e^{\alpha\beta_{i}}}{e^{\alpha\beta_{i}}+K-1}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, it holds that</p>
<table id="A6.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex88.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}}+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}}+K-2}{(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}})(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}})}(\frac{e^{\alpha\beta_{2}}}{(K-1)(K-1+e^{\alpha\beta_{2}})}+\frac{K-2}{K-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}}+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}}+K-2}{(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}})(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}})}(\frac{e^{\alpha\beta_{2}}}{(K-1)(K-1+e^{\alpha\beta_{2}})}+\frac{K-2}{K-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}})(K-1+e^{\alpha\beta_{2}})}(\frac{e^{\alpha^{\prime}(\beta_{1}+\beta_{2})}+K-1}{K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}}})-\frac{1}{K}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}})(K-1+e^{\alpha\beta_{2}})}(\frac{e^{\alpha^{\prime}(\beta_{1}+\beta_{2})}+K-1}{K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}}})-\frac{1}{K}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Notice that when <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(0,\beta_{2})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(0,\beta_{2})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. We now calculate the partial derivative of <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. It holds that</p>
<table id="A6.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial g}{\partial\beta_{1}}=\frac{\alpha^{\prime}e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}}(e^{\alpha\beta_{2}}-1)(1-e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}})}{(K-1+e^{\alpha\beta_{2}})(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}})(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}})^{2}}\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial g}{\partial\beta_{1}}=\frac{\alpha^{\prime}e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}}(e^{\alpha\beta_{2}}-1)(1-e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}})}{(K-1+e^{\alpha\beta_{2}})(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}})(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}})^{2}}\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.6" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we know that <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})\leq g(0,\beta_{2})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})\leq g(0,\beta_{2})=0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> holding for any difficulties <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. By symmetry, it suffices to average over the other agents, which does not alter the fact that the expected advantage of ISP remains greater than that of MV. We hence conclude that <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[Adv_{ISP}(s^{*})]\geq\mathbb{E}[Adv_{MV}(s^{*})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[Adv_{ISP}(s^{*})]\geq\mathbb{E}[Adv_{MV}(s^{*})]</annotation></semantics></math> similar as the proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 4.2 From Surprisingly Popular to Inverse Surprisingly Popular ‣ 4 Leveraging Second-order Information ‣ Beyond Majority Voting: LLM Aggregation by Leveraging Higher-Order Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, when we compare MV with SP, we only need to prove</p>
<table id="A6.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex91.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{2}(\alpha)[x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime})x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime})+\frac{(1-x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime}))(1-x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime}))}{K-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{2}(\alpha)[x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime})x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime})+\frac{(1-x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime}))(1-x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime}))}{K-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+(1-x_{2}(\alpha))[\frac{x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime})(1-x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime}))+(1-x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime}))x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime})}{K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(1-x_{2}(\alpha))[\frac{x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime})(1-x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime}))+(1-x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime}))x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime})}{K-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{K-2}{(K-1)^{2}}(1-x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime})(1-x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime})))]-\frac{1}{K}\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{K-2}{(K-1)^{2}}(1-x_{1}(\alpha^{\prime})(1-x_{2}(\alpha^{\prime})))]-\frac{1}{K}\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">It then holds that</p>
<table id="A6.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex94.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{e^{\alpha\beta_{2}}}{K-1+e^{\alpha\beta_{2}}}\frac{e^{\alpha^{\prime}(\beta_{1}+\beta_{2})}+K-1}{(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}})(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{e^{\alpha\beta_{2}}}{K-1+e^{\alpha\beta_{2}}}\frac{e^{\alpha^{\prime}(\beta_{1}+\beta_{2})}+K-1}{(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}})(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{K-1}{K-1+e^{\alpha\beta_{2}}}\frac{e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}}+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}}+K-2}{(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}})(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}})}-\frac{1}{K}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{K-1}{K-1+e^{\alpha\beta_{2}}}\frac{e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}}+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}}+K-2}{(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}})(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}})}-\frac{1}{K}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Notice that when <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(0,\beta_{2})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(0,\beta_{2})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. In addition, with some calculations, it holds that</p>
<table id="A6.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial h}{\partial\beta_{1}}=\frac{\alpha^{\prime}e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}}(K-1)(e^{\alpha\beta_{2}}-1)(e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}}-1)}{(K-1+e^{\alpha\beta_{2}})(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}})(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}})^{2}}\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial h}{\partial\beta_{1}}=\frac{\alpha^{\prime}e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}}(K-1)(e^{\alpha\beta_{2}}-1)(e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}}-1)}{(K-1+e^{\alpha\beta_{2}})(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{2}})(K-1+e^{\alpha^{\prime}\beta_{1}})^{2}}\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we know that <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})\geq h(0,\beta_{2})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})\geq h(0,\beta_{2})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[Adv_{SP}(s^{*})]\leq\mathbb{E}[Adv_{MV}(s^{*})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[Adv_{SP}(s^{*})]\leq\mathbb{E}[Adv_{MV}(s^{*})]</annotation></semantics></math> due to the linearity of expectation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Despite the difficulty of questions being unknown in general LLM reasoning settings, ISP still enjoys a larger expected advantage compared to majority voting. This demonstrates the robustness of our approach in more general scenarios and highlights its broad applicability.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
